"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nEvery stable version of 4.x\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10, Ryzen 4650G with integrated Vega7 igpu, Vulkan support, 16GB DDR4 ram\n\n### Issue description\n\nSorry for my poor english, i try to describe the issue. When i try to import a larger scene, modell file with hundreds of meshes, the editor always crash. It isn't a new problem.  I use godot from 3.0 and it exist in all 4.x version (maybe in 3.x too, i don't test it nowadays), but it's an old godot problem. I know that some streamer can import these model files without crash, so my thought is that the low igpu, with shared memory can cause this problem, but im not sure. The size of modell files doesn't matter in MB. The type of file (dae, fbx, glb or blender) doesn't matter too. I can't import with my hardware a 3MB small modell files too, if there are 600 low poly meshes inside of it. Maybe the mesh streaming will fix this issue, or i don't know, but i thought i write here to give a report of it. Thanks.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI know this step is hilarous, but i can't write anything else. I can't test with a good gpu.\n\nTry import this with an igpu (without huge memory of dedicated video card):\nhttps://elbolilloduro.itch.io/paquete-de-modelos-psx-3\n(the \"All.fbx\")\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":{"login":"thottee","id":42456553,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNDU2NTUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42456553?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thottee","html_url":"https://github.com/thottee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thottee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thottee/following{/other_user}","gists_url"